{
  "category": "Weed Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "During the day, it keeps its face buried in the ground. At night, it wanders around sowing its seeds.",
      "version": "red"
    },
    {
      "text": "During the day, it keeps its face buried in the ground. At night, it wanders around sowing its seeds.",
      "version": "blue"
    },
    {
      "text": "It may be mistaken for a clump of weeds. If you try to yank it out of the ground, it shrieks horribly.",
      "version": "yellow"
    },
    {
      "text": "Awakened by moonlight, it roams actively at night. In the day, it stays quietly underground.",
      "version": "gold"
    },
    {
      "text": "If exposed to moonlight, it starts to move. It roams far and wide at night to scatter its seeds.",
      "version": "silver"
    },
    {
      "text": "During the day, it stays in the cold underground to avoid the sun. It grows by bathing in moonlight.",
      "version": "crystal"
    },
    {
      "text": "During the daytime, ODDISH buries itself in soil to absorb nutrients from the ground using its entire body. The more fertile the soil, the glossier its leaves become.",
      "version": "ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "ODDISH searches for fertile, nutrient- rich soil, then plants itself. During the daytime, while it is planted, this POKéMON’s feet are thought to change shape and become similar to the roots of trees.",
      "version": "sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "This POKéMON grows by absorbing moonlight. During the daytime, it buries itself in the ground, leaving only its leaves exposed to avoid detection by its enemies.",
      "version": "emerald"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its scientific name is “Oddium Wanderus.” At night, it is said to walk nearly 1,000 feet on its two roots.",
      "version": "firered"
    },
    {
      "text": "During the day, it keeps its face buried in the ground. At night, it wanders around sowing its seeds.",
      "version": "leafgreen"
    },
    {
      "text": "It often plants its root feet in the ground during the day and sows seeds as it walks about at night.",
      "version": "diamond"
    },
    {
